&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Raisin UK Finance team is expanding, and we are looking for a hands-on, commercially astute &lt;strong&gt;Senior Finance Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Manchester office. Working directly alongside the Head of Finance UK, this is a high-impact individual contributor role designed for an autonomous operator who thrives on ownership, commercial variety, and cross-functional leadership. With a primary emphasis on FP&amp;amp;A and commercial growth, you will bridge strategic forecasting, business partnering, financial reporting, and process automation in a fast-growing fintech scale-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Reporting, Controlling &amp;amp; Audit Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the preparation of timely, high-accuracy monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements in accordance with UK GAAP/ IFRS, alongside insightful internal management reporting packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead core operational accounting workflows, including revenue invoicing, reconciliations, and balance sheet integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, establish, and continuously enhance internal financial controls, governance workflows, and accounting procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key operational point of contact for internal and external auditors, ensuring smooth, efficient audit cycles and statutory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ad-hoc financial evaluations and commercial business cases requested by local executive leadership and central Group Finance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Business Development (BD) and Relationship Managers (RMs) to model, anticipate, and stress-test future Assets on Platform (AoP) volumes, evaluate growth bottlenecks, and unlock new revenue expansion opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess end-to-end knowledge of core accounting functions to provide seamless interim coverage and operational backfill across the finance team when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Planning, Forecasting &amp;amp; Commercial Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive regular financial forecasting cycles, variance analyses, and the annual budgeting process for the UK business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular, actionable analyses of trading performance, unit economics, and underlying revenue trends to inform operational strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ad-hoc financial and commercial analyses requested by local leadership and central Group Finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Business Partnering &amp;amp; System Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted finance partner to commercial teams and operational leaders, guiding budget holders on spend optimization, ROI, and resource allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion financial process automation and AI adoption—leveraging modern workflow tools and AI-driven solutions to automate reporting, revenue recognition, invoicing, and billing cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the ongoing evolution of our controlling systems landscape and internal reporting architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion financial process automation—particularly around revenue recognition, invoicing, and billing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support local rollout and implementation of group-wide finance tools and enterprise systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 4+ years of progressive experience in roles such as Financial Controller, Senior Management Accountant, or FP&amp;amp;A / Controlling, ideally within a scaling fintech, tech platform, or dynamic high-growth business. Equally ideal opportunity for anyone currently operating at a Managerial grade within a Big 4 accounting/audit firm and considering a change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Professional Foundation:&lt;/strong&gt; University degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related discipline. A recognized professional accounting qualification (ACA, ACCA, CIMA) is a distinct advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep practical understanding of UK GAAP; working knowledge of IFRS is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Modeling Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong quantitative mindset with advanced financial modeling capabilities, high attention to detail, and a structured, self-directed working style.&lt;/li&gt;
